  "problem": "The equation ${x}^{2}+12x+108=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q$, and solve the equation.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p+q\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,x=-6\\,\\pm \\,\\text{i}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x+108 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x & =-108\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x & =-108 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ (x+6)^{2}-36 & =-108 \\\\ (x+6)^{2} & =-72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=6,q=-72,$ and $p+q=-66.$\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2} & =-72 \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-72} \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-36\\cdot 2} \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm 6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-6\\pm \\text{i}\\,6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-6+6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-6-6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.$",
